// =============================================================================
// Data-classification annotations.
//
// WHY THIS FILE IS THE MOST IMPORTANT ONE IN contracts/:
//
// India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 obliges us to know exactly
// which fields carry personal data, where they flow, and how long we keep them.
// Answering that with a spreadsheet is how compliance programmes fail — the
// spreadsheet drifts from the code within one sprint.
//
// Instead we classify data AT THE SCHEMA LEVEL. Every field carrying personal
// data is annotated here, and that annotation is machine-readable. The platform
// libraries (packages/go/platform, packages/python/platform) read these
// annotations off the protobuf descriptor at runtime to drive, automatically:
//
//   1. Log redaction        — annotated fields never reach a log sink verbatim.
//   2. Retention enforcement — the retention class drives deletion jobs.
//   3. Residency routing     — data classified as personal must not leave the
//                              India region (Phase 1 assumption A2).
//   4. Data-map generation   — docs/compliance/data-map is generated, not typed.
//
// This makes privacy a property of the schema rather than a discipline the
// engineer has to remember at every call site.
// =============================================================================

